Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Spec 34: number methods, std::bit_cast,
 std::meta::type_id, std::assume, std::unreachable

- f32/f64: sqrt, abs, floor, ceil, round, trunc, min, max, clamp, mul_add, sin, cos, tan,
  asin, acos, atan, atan2, exp, exp2, log, log2, log10, pow, copysign, is_nan/infinite/finite;
  integers: abs (checked), min, max, clamp; also at compile time
- unknown methods on numbers, bool and char are now an error (were silently accepted)
- std::bit_cast<T>(x): safe between plain-bit types of the same size
- std::raw::assume/unreachable intrinsics; std::assume/std::unreachable checked in safe modes
- calls of functions returning never end the block (fixes a crash)

